DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  iiccoonnvv(3)  function internally uses _g_c_o_n_v modules to convert to and
       from a character set.  A configuration file is used  to  determine  the
       needed modules for a conversion.  Loading and parsing such a configura‐
       tion  file  would  slow  down  programs that use iiccoonnvv(3), so a caching
       mechanism is employed.

       The iiccoonnvvccoonnffiigg program reads  iconv  module  configuration  files  and
       writes a fast‐loading gconv module configuration cache file.

       In  addition to the system provided gconv modules, the user can specify
       custom  gconv  module  directories  with   the   environment   variable
       GGCCOONNVV__PPAATTHH.   However,  iconv module configuration caching is used only
       when the environment variable GGCCOONNVV__PPAATTHH is not set.

